# Static assets, CDNs, and soft-nav

Several agents work on this repo. Follow these rules every time — they are also
in `AGENTS.md` and enforced by `tests/test_asset_cache_bust.py` + `.githooks/pre-commit`.

## Content-hashed static URLs

- Templates: `{{ asset('file.css') }}` (or `url_for('static', ...)` — hashed via
  `@app.url_defaults`).
- NEVER hand-write `?v=34`, `?v=2`, `?ver=`, or `?t=<date>`. That pattern caused
  repeated production incidents (`sales_report.css?v=19`, then ~847 pins).
- JS string URLs in templates: `{{ asset('file.js')|tojson }}`.

## No public CDN for app JS/CSS

- Vendor libraries under `static/` and load with `asset()`. Lucide is
  `static/lucide.min.js`.
- Do not add `unpkg.com`, `jsdelivr`, `cdnjs`, or `@latest` script tags. They
  hang entire modules (Payroll, Access Management) when the CDN stalls.
- Google Fonts CSS with `display=swap` is fine; never pull JS from a font CDN.

## Soft-nav HTML prefetch

- Do not add heavy modules to `IDLE_PREFETCH_PATHS` (only `/home`,
  `/main-dashboard`, `/master`, `/settings`, `/license`).
- Restaurant/Bar Tables/Invoice/Menu shells must stay **prefetchable** for
  instant open. Only mutation lists (invoice-ledger, sales-update, settings,
  payroll, access, accounts, stores, communication) are live-only — never a
  blanket `/point-of-sale` live-only prefix.
- Soft-nav cache is build-bound via `syncSoftNavBuildId` / `/hbe-build.json`.
- Keep `clearSoftNavPrefetch()` on SW/build-id reload paths in `de_pwa.js`.
- After Home, `scheduleCriticalModuleWarm()` idle-warms Restaurant/Bar/Hotel.
- Self-host fonts via `partials/hbe_fonts.html` / `hbe_login_fonts.html` — never
  `fonts.googleapis.com`.

## Guard

If `tests/test_asset_cache_bust.py` fails, fix the template/JS — do not weaken
the test.
